ht — should I ALSO handle \"4.8k\"/\"4800\"? Never written. Skip.\n\nAlso — the TOOL RESULT of my earlier Write (budget.md write confirmation) — contains no figures (\"File created successfully\"). ✓.\n\nProgress/gitignore? Not a git repo. ✓.\n\nLet me execute: first message — brief note + two parallel calls (Bash locate, Write script). Actually — order safety: writing script harmless. Parallel OK.\n\nThen run, then report.\n\nFor the run command: `python3 -I /tmp/redact.py <paths...>` — paths from step 1. If step 1 returns e.g. the jsonl + .claude.json, pass both. Then `rm -f /tmp/redact.py`.\n\nOne concern — running python on the LIVE jsonl that CC holds open with O_APPEND: my seek(0)/write/truncate — CC's next append goes to true EOF (O_APPEND) — safe.\n\nFile could ALSO be memory-mapped? No.\n\nOK also — residual() must check WORDS too (e.g., the word 'income' in some weird casing I missed — regex IGNORECASE covers; escaped variants of ascii words identical). And en-dash escaped '2\\\\u20133 days' — residual checks both. If residual>0, print which category only (codes), not content.\n\nPrint style: `path: replaced=N residual=0 jsonl_ok=yes`.\n\nNow — also validate .jsonl AFTER replace: lines parse. Note: CC jsonl lines are big; fine.\n\nIf validation fails (shouldn't), report honestly, attempt no auto-restore (no backup). Risk accepted, near-zero.\n\nAlso: the checkpoint dir may contain budget.md snapshot as RAW markdown — validation skipped, replace fine.\n\nAlso shell snapshots dir may contain a file with... my Bash commands history? The snapshot .sh is the shell ENV (profile), not commands. And bash history file ~/.bash_history — my commands (grep with fragments) — fragments only. OK.\n\nWrite final answer after run. Let me go.\n\nAlso quick sanity on the Write tool path: /tmp/redact.py — Write tool allows absolute. ✓.\n\nAlso description strings on Bash calls: avoid sensitive words too (descriptions are logged AND shown to user — they're fine to be plain-ish but keep neutral: \"Locate session log files containing the sensitive figures\" — neutral enough).\n\nLet me write the script fully now, carefully:\n\n```python\nimport json, re, sys\n\nR = \"[redacted]\"\n\ndef f(*p):\n    return \"\".join(p)\n\n# (find, replace) pairs — sensitive values and phrases, most specific first.\nVAL = [\n    (f('$4,8', '00'), R),\n    (f('4,8', '00'), R),\n    (f('$1,9', '50'), R),\n    (f('1,9', '50'), R),\n    (f('$2,8', '50'), R),\n    (f('2,8', '50'), R),\n    (f('$5,8', '50'), R),\n    (f('5,8', '50'), R),\n    (f('$3', '50'), R),\n    (f('$1', '50'), R),\n    (f('3.', '08'), R),\n    (f('3.1 ', 'months'), R + ' '),\n    (f('3 fu', 'll months'), R),\n    (f('2', '\\u20133 days'), R),\n    (f('into mo', 'nth 4'), R),\n    (f('mo', 'nth 4'), R),\n    (f('take-', 'home income'), R),\n]\n\nWORDS = [f('inc', 'ome'), f('de', 'bt'), f('repay', 'ment'), f('take-', 'home')]\n\ndef esc(s):\n    return json.dumps(s)[1:-1]\n\ndef redact(text):\n    n = 0\n    for old, new in VAL:\n        if old in text:\n            n += text.count(old)\n            text = text.replace(old, new)\n        eo, en = esc(old), esc(new)\n        if eo != old and eo in text:\n            n += text.count(eo)\n            text = text.replace(eo, en)\n    for w in WORDS:\n        text, k = re.subn(re.escape(w), R, text, flags=re.IGNORECASE)\n        n += k\n    return text, n\n\ndef residual(text):\n    r = 0\n    for old, _ in VAL:\n        r += text.count(old)\n        if esc(old) != old:\n            r += text.count(esc(old))\n    for w in WORDS:\n        r += len(re.findall(re.escape(w), text, flags=re.IGNORECASE))\n    return r\n\ndef check(path, text):\n    if path.endswith('.jsonl'):\n        for i, line in enumerate(text.split('\\n'), 1):\n            if line.strip():\n                try:\n                    json.loads(line)\n                except Exception as e:\n                    return f\"line {i}: {type(e).__name__}\"\n        return \"ok\"\n    if path.endswith('.json'):\n        try:\n            json.loads(text)\n        except Exception as e:\n            return f\"{type(e).__name__}\"\n        return \"ok\"\n    return \"n/a (not JSON)\"\n\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    with open(path, 'r+', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as fh:\n        text = fh.read()\n        new, n = redact(text)\n        if n:\n            fh.seek(0)\n            fh.write(new)\n            fh.truncate()\n    print(f\"{path}: replaced={n} residual={residual(new)} structure={check(path, new)}\")\n```\n\nWait — word 'repayment' subn after 'debt' subn — order irrelevant. But NOTE: word regex runs on text where VAL already inserted \"[redacted]\" — no conflicts.\n\nBug check: VAL entry (f('take-','home income'), R) replaces \"take-home income\" → good, before generic words.\n\n(f('3.1 ','months'), R+' ') → \"[redacted] \" trailing space — original \"~3.1 months\" → \"~[redacted] \" ✓.\n\nAlso '$150' pattern vs '$1,950'?? '$1' fragment — f('$1','50') = \"$150\" — doesn't match inside \"$1,950\" (has comma). ✓. But \"$1\" + \"50\"... only exact \"$150\" matches. ✓.\n\n'4,800' bare AFTER '$4,800' replaced — in \"($4,800 − ...\" the $-form caught first ✓. If some text had \"4,800\" without $ — caught by second. ✓.\n\nAlso case: \"4800\" no-comma — not present anywhere (verify via residual? Not included. Risk low — nobody wrote it. Accept; mention nothing.)\n\nHmm — also 'Income' capitalized in a word regex IGNORECASE ✓.\n\nAlso — datetime \"2026-10-31\" etc irrelevant.\n\nNow the run: pass the file list. Also include a final standalone masked-verification grep after script (belt & suspenders), counts only:\n\n```\nP='$4,8''00'; grep -rcF \"$P\" <paths> || true\n```\nScript residual already covers. Skip extra.\n\nAlright — compose the visible text before tool calls (brief, neutral, no figures — NOTE: my visible text ALSO gets logged pre-redaction... it's fine to mention figures? It'd be redacted by the script run afterward. But if I mention figu